WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.490
What a chatbot reads before your message

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:06.242
Before your message, a chatbot
is given text you don’t see.

3
00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:09.455
A system prompt setting
its tone and rules,

4
00:00:09.455 --> 00:00:14.088
information about each tool it can use
and descriptions of skills –

5
00:00:14.088 --> 00:00:19.175
instruction files it can load when
necessary for tasks like website design.

6
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.036
With memory switched on, it also gets
short notes about you from past chats.

7
00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:26.988
These can change its replies
in obvious ways,

8
00:00:26.988 --> 00:00:30.653
like giving examples related to your job
and subtle ones

9
00:00:30.653 --> 00:00:34.657
like using red in all its designs
because you work at LSE.

10
00:00:34.657 --> 00:00:37.934
You can also add your own layers
through global preferences

11
00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:42.779
and custom instructions for things like
Claude Projects or Copilot Agents.

12
00:00:43.322 --> 00:00:46.882
Alongside the harness –
the software around the model –

13
00:00:46.882 --> 00:00:50.444
these hidden layers are another reason
the same model can act differently

14
00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:54.220
in different apps, and the prompt
layers are all processed

15
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.335
again with every message along
with the whole chat so far.

16
00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:02.008
In addition to the fact that normal
chats now use tools in a loop

17
00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:05.349
like coding agents, these
increased layers of prompts

18
00:01:05.349 --> 00:01:09.712
are another reason chatbots now use
far more tokens than they used to.

19
00:01:09.712 --> 00:01:12.675
Try this: in a normal chat, ask

20
00:01:12.675 --> 00:01:14.472
“What do you know about me?”

21
00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:18.010
Then in the chatbot’s memory settings,
remove anything out of date

22
00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.786
or that you don’t want to shape
the replies it gives you.

23
00:01:20.786 --> 00:01:23.832
Compare the same prompts in incognito
mode and a normal chat

24
00:01:23.832 --> 00:01:27.366
to see the difference that
memory features make.
